 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "2019-05-21",
   "text": "Medical Debt Relief Act of 2019\n This bill modifies requirements related to the reporting of medical debt. Specifically, a consumer reporting agency may not add certain medical debt information to a consumer credit report. Also, a debt collector may not report certain medical debt information to a consumer reporting agency within a specified time period and must notify the consumer prior to reporting such medical debt."
  }
 ],
